The degradation comes from one slow call path, search→geo, and it reaches users through search and frontend. I'm naming a single fault at `search`.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT src, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.5) p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) p95_ms FROM (SELECT 'abn' src,* FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'norm',* FROM normal_traces) WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name IN ('geo.Geo/Nearby','rate.Rate/GetRates','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 ORDER BY 3,1", "claim": "search's client call to geo.Geo/Nearby rises from ~0.37ms to ~1576ms p50, while its rate calls stay ~1.7ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT src, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.5) p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) p95_ms FROM (SELECT 'abn' src,* FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'norm',* FROM normal_traces) WHERE service_name='geo' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4", "claim": "geo's own server spans for geo.Geo/Nearby stay around 0.14ms p50 in both periods, so geo is not the slow party."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT src, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.5) p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.95) p95_ms FROM (SELECT 'abn' src,* FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'norm',* FROM normal_traces) WHERE (service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('HTTP /hotels','search.Search/Nearby')) OR (service_name='search' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 ORDER BY 2,3,1", "claim": "search.Search/Nearby server p50 rises from ~1.8ms to ~1578ms, and frontend HTTP /hotels p50 rises from ~4.6ms to ~1583ms."}]}
  ]
}
```

